# data-models-relationships

Core Data Models:

1. Case Management Model
- Hierarchical structure for managing social work cases
- Real-time integration with resource databases
- Relationship mapping between cases and local resources
- Prioritization system based on urgency levels
File: components/CaseManagementClient.tsx

2. Knowledge Base Structure
- Domain-specific categorization for social work practices
- Hierarchical organization of treatment protocols
- Relationship mapping between best practices and resources
File: components/knowledge/BestPracticesManager.tsx

3. Resource Database Schema
- Integration with 211 social services database
- Local resource mapping and relationships
- Service capability classifications
- Geographic proximity relationships
Path: app/api/generate-plan/stream/route.ts

4. Professional Development Model
- Organizational knowledge hierarchy
- Resource type classifications (worksheet, reading, exercise)
- Relationship mapping to best practices
Path: app/api/generate-skill-resource/route.ts

Key Relationships:

1. Case-Resource Mapping
- Cases link to multiple local resources
- Resources categorized by service type
- Priority-based relationship weighting
- Geographic service area relationships

2. Knowledge-Practice Integration  
- Best practices link to multiple resources
- Hierarchical categorization relationships
- Domain-specific protocol mappings
- Evidence-based practice relationships

3. Client-Resource Connections
- Client needs mapping to resource types
- Accessibility-based relationship scoring
- Trauma-informed content relationships
Path: app/api/generate-client-resource/route.ts

